      "type": "feat",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<p>The giblin launches itself 50 feet in a straight line. <em>Saving Throw:</em> DC 13 Dexterity, each creature in the giblin's path. <em>Failure:</em> 7 (2d6) Bludgeoning damage, and if the creature is Medium or smaller, it is knocked Prone.</p><p>If no creatures fail the save or if the giblin's movement ends early due to a wall or other obstruction, the giblin crashes, taking 7 (2d6) Bludgeoning damage and knocking itself Prone.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
